<section id="play">
  <p class="hint">Read once, properly. Most losses are operator error, not bad data.</p>

  <details><summary>Data classes and what they actually trade for</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>CC + exp + CVV only</b> &mdash; $1&ndash;8. Disposable.</li>
      <li><b>+ name / address / zip</b> &mdash; AVS-capable, $8&ndash;18.</li>
      <li><b>+ SSN / DOB / MMN</b> &mdash; full fullz, $15&ndash;40.</li>
      <li><b>+ email or bank login (a "log")</b> &mdash; premium, because it beats OTP.</li>
      <li><b>Session cookies</b> &mdash; highest value. A live session skips 3DS entirely.</li>
      <li><b>Non-VBV / auto-VBV BIN</b> &mdash; the only thing that matters for volume. A perfect card on a 3DS-locked BIN is paper.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Keystroke logs and clipboard are how you find the OTP window and the email password. Never cash a card whose BIN you haven't checked.</p>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Validation before you touch anything</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>BIN lookup first.</b> Card type, level, country, bank, 3DS enrolment. If it's 3DS/OTP, park it unless you hold the email.</li>
      <li><b>Live check</b> &mdash; $0.50&ndash;1 auth on a merchant with soft declines. "Live" means approved <i>and</i> AVS response captured.</li>
      <li><b>AVS</b> &mdash; full match or full non-avs only. Partial match is merchant lottery.</li>
      <li><b>Geo</b> &mdash; proxy state must equal cardholder state. Same city is better. Different country is a dead card.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Cashout routes, easiest to hardest</summary><div class="in">
    <p><span class="tag">low value</span> <b>Gift cards / digital goods</b> &mdash; Amazon, Apple, Steam, Netflix. Instant, one shot, 40&ndash;60% resale. Burns the card immediately; good for clearing volume.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">low risk</span> <b>Bill pay / utilities</b> &mdash; near-zero decline rate, thin margin. Good for laundering small balances.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">needs identity</span> <b>PayPal / Cash App sends</b> &mdash; needs a warmed account and a fullz. Dies in hours.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">high ticket</span> <b>Flights and hotels</b> &mdash; biggest single tickets, needs exact identity match. Non-refundable, so one mistake is total loss.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">best resale</span> <b>Physical goods to a drop</b> &mdash; 70&ndash;85%. Drop address in the cardholder's state, 3&ndash;7 days to land.</p>
    <p><span class="tag">hardware</span> <b>ATM with a cloned card</b> &mdash; best per-card return, needs MSR605X + blanks. PIN comes from track 2 or the fullz.</p>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Operating rules that decide the outcome</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li><b>One card, one merchant, one session.</b> Never a second order on a used card.</li>
      <li><b>Residential SOCKS5 in the cardholder's state.</b> Datacenter IPs are flagged by every decent fraud engine.</li>
      <li><b>Fresh antidetect profile per card.</b> Timezone, UA, WebRTC, canvas must agree with the proxy.</li>
      <li><b>Billing exactly as on file.</b> Shipping can be a drop; billing cannot be guessed.</li>
      <li><b>Stay under $300</b> on a merchant you haven't worked. Above that is manual review.</li>
      <li><b>Two to four orders per hour</b> per IP block. Faster looks like a bot.</li>
      <li><b>Use your own catch-all email</b> on the order, never the victim's &mdash; the victim can't cancel what they can't see.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Kill signals &mdash; when to walk away</summary><div class="in">
    <ul>
      <li>Three consecutive declines on one card: card dead or IP burned. Stop.</li>
      <li><span class="bad">Do not honor</span> &mdash; velocity or geo mismatch. Change proxy before retrying.</li>
      <li><span class="warn">AVS mismatch</span> &mdash; move to an AVS-off merchant.</li>
      <li>Bank suddenly pushes OTP &mdash; BIN is 3DS-locked. Park it, don't burn attempts.</li>
      <li>Merchant shows a captcha on checkout &mdash; profile is dirty. Rebuild it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>The 24-hour rule and your first hour</summary><div class="in">
    <p>Card half-life is hours to days, and it's shortest on the best BINs because everyone hits them. Sort your batch by BIN quality the moment a package lands, and cash the top three inside the first hour. Everything below the line gets sold as logs instead of worked.</p>
    <p>First hour, in order: decrypt package &rarr; BIN-check every card &rarr; tag non-VBV &rarr; pull matching proxies &rarr; work the top three &rarr; sell the remainder.</p>
  </div></details>

  <details><summary>Sell or cash?</summary><div class="in">
    <p>Selling logs on Telegram markets returns 30&ndash;50% of face with no tooling. Cashing returns more but needs proxies, an antidetect browser, drop addresses and checker credits. Correct first move: sell the first batch, buy the tooling out of it, then start cashing. Don't cash on a residential connection with a stock browser.</p>
  </div></details>
</section>

<section id="opsec">
  <p class="hint">Tap to tick. Persists on this device only.</p>
  <div id="chk"></div>
  <hr>
  <div class="card"><h3>TRACK COVERING</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Bot on a <b>burner Telegram account</b> and a second SIM or eSIM. Never your real number.</li>
      <li>Every upload goes out with <code>protect_content</code> set &mdash; no forwarding, no saving from chat.</li>
      <li>Pull loot to phone storage and open it in place. Don't forward it to Saved Messages.</li>
      <li><b>Rotate the bot token</b> between campaigns. In direct mode anyone holding an old exe holds your token.</li>
      <li>Worker mode keeps the token off the binary; rotate the HMAC secret to kill old builds without rebuilding.</li>
      <li>Delete the bot with <code>/deletebot</code> when a campaign closes.</li>
      <li>Zip password never goes in the same channel as the zip.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card"><h3>PAYLOAD HYGIENE</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>One exe per campaign, never recycled across targets.</li>
      <li>Rebuild from a fresh repo so the artifact has no shared history.</li>
      <li>Expect Defender flags &mdash; "More info &rarr; Run anyway" is the script for the target.</li>
      <li>Check the VM flag in <code>info.json</code>. <code>VM</code> means you're on a sandbox and the sample may have been detonated.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

